      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can we be sure that no vendor modules ever read/write the old version of the modified fields? You have to assume that vendor modules might have been built before this change. If this really is safe, and wireless_dev is managed carefully (eg, allocated in place and not embedded in other structs), perhaps you could do something like:\n```\nstruct wireless_dev_ext {\n  struct wireless_dev wireless_dev;\n  struct wiphy_work wiphy work;\n}\n```\nand access wiphy_work by using `container_of()` on the given wireless_dev. I haven\u0027t looked to see if this could actually work in your case. I\u0027ll try a little harder after you convince me that it is safe to assume that it is safe to assume that drivers never use wdev-\u003epmsr_free_wk.",
